{
  "name": "Latin American Studies - BA - Mexico",
  "kind": "major",
  "type": "Bachelor's Degree",
  "department": "Latin American Studies",
  "source": "https://catalog.ucsd.edu/curric/LATI-ug.html",
  "narrative": [
    "To satisfactorily complete the BA, students must complete fifty-six credit units.",
    "All the elective courses (including the research methods course) must be upper-division courses.",
    "All courses applied to the requirements of the major must be taken for a letter grade and students must earn at least a C- in each course counted for the major, with the exception of LATI 199 and the one-unit discussion seminars, which will be graded as Pass/Not Pass.",
    "Language courses do not count toward the course requirements for Latin American studies degrees.",
    "Up to six upper-division courses in the major can be petitioned for credit from EAP/OAP study abroad.",
    "AIP 197 can be counted as one of the elective courses required by the Latin American studies major.",
    "Students are strongly encouraged to consider the possibility of enrolling in LATI 199: Individual Study and/or AIP 197: Academic Internship Program (recommendation)."
  ],
